    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch06-item-1-1-1",
      "sourceStart": 533,
      "sourceEnd": 758,
      "original": "#### 1.1.1. <span style=\"color: red\">(Inner product)</span> An inner product on $V$ is a function that takes each ordered pair $(u,v)$ of elements of $V$ to a number $\\langle u,v\\rangle\\in F$ and has the following properties.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch06-block-0004",
      "sourceStart": 758,
      "sourceEnd": 1264,
      "sha256": "dadb8c41b165c4f8b6b5c572e2f010ff5090b8cf1763c0a4901b9d9847ebba42"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch06-item-1-1-2",
      "sourceStart": 1264,
      "sourceEnd": 1358,
      "original": "#### 1.1.2. <span style=\"color: red\">(Norm)</span> For $v\\in V$, the norm of $v$ is defined by",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch06-block-0005",
      "sourceStart": 1358,
      "sourceEnd": 1401,
      "sha256": "f7fed03f4a97ba54ae5530aad27558948f97ada1e95dc8cf669117fc2e8113ed"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch06-item-1-1-3",
      "sourceStart": 1401,
      "sourceEnd": 1490,
      "original": "#### 1.1.3. Two vectors $v,w \\in V$ are called **orthogonal** if $\\langle v,w \\rangle=0$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
