    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch06-item-1-3-3",
      "sourceStart": 2472,
      "sourceEnd": 2706,
      "original": "#### 1.3.3. <span style=\"color: red\">(Pseudoinverse)</span> Suppose $V,W$ are finite-dimensional inner product spaces and $T\\in\\mathcal{L}(V,W)$. The **pseudoinverse** $T^{\\dagger}\\in\\mathcal{L}(W,V)$ of $T$ is a linear map defined by",
