      "sha256": "c475894e72d44da53b652f55dd2316afd2bff1e9ee8f1b303c355b03ad8306be"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch06-item-2-2-5",
      "sourceStart": 5106,
      "sourceEnd": 5391,
      "original": "#### 2.2.5. Suppose $V$ is finite-dimensional inner product space and $T\\in \\mathcal{L}(V)$. Then $T$ has an upper-triangular matrix representation with respect to some orthonormal basis if and only if the minimal polynomial of $T$ is in the form of $(z-\\lambda_1)\\cdots(z-\\lambda_m)$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
